XBOARD(1)                                               XBOARD(1)


               plays black.  Default: "gnuchessr".

       --ssccpp oorr --sseeccoonnddCChheessssPPrrooggrraamm pprrooggrraamm
               Name of second chess  program  that,  by  default,
               plays white.  Default: "gnuchessr".

       --ffhh oorr --ffiirrssttHHoosstt hhoosstt
               Name  of  host  the  white chess program plays on.
               Default: "localhost".

       --sshh oorr --sseeccoonnddHHoosstt hhoosstt
               Name of host the black  chess  program  plays  on.
               Default: "localhost".

       --ss**bb oorr --ssoolliidd**BBiittmmaapp ffiillee
               Names  of  the  bitmap  files for the bitmap piece
               icons.         Default:         solid_pawn.bitmap,
               solid_rook.bitmap ...

       --oo**bb oorr --oouuttlliinnee**BBiittmmaapp ffiillee
               Names  of  the  bitmap files for the outline piece
               icons.    Default:    outline_pawn.bitmap,    out-
               line_rook.bitmap ...

       --mmmm oorr --mmaattcchhMMooddee ((FFaallssee || IInniitt || PPoossiittiioonn || OOppeenniinngg))
               Automatically run a game between _f_i_r_s_t_C_h_e_s_s_P_r_o_g_r_a_m
               and _s_e_c_o_n_d_C_h_e_s_s_P_r_o_g_r_a_m.  If _m_a_t_c_h_M_o_d_e  is  set  to
               _I_n_i_t,  _x_b_o_a_r_d will start the game with the initial
               chess position.  If _m_a_t_c_h_M_o_d_e is set to  _P_o_s_i_t_i_o_n,
               _x_b_o_a_r_d will start the game with the position spec-
               ified by the _r_e_a_d_P_o_s_i_t_i_o_n_F_i_l_e resource.  If _m_a_t_c_h_-
               _M_o_d_e  is  set to _O_p_e_n_i_n_g, _x_b_o_a_r_d will play out the
               opening  moves  specified  by  the   _-_r_e_a_d_G_a_m_e_F_i_l_e
               resource.  Default: "False".

       --mmoonnoo oorr --mmoonnooMMooddee ((FFaallssee || TTrruuee))
               Determines  whether _x_b_o_a_r_d displays its pieces and
               squares with two colors or  four.   You  shouldn't
               have to specify monochrome.  _x_b_o_a_r_d will determine
               if this is necessary.

RREESSOOUURRCCEESS
       iinniittSSttrriinngg
               The actual string that is sent to  initialize  the
               chess  program  can  be  set  from .Xdefaults.  It
               can't be set from the command line because of syn-
               tax problems.

       wwhhiitteeSSttrriinngg aanndd bbllaacckkSSttrriinngg
               These  resources  control  what  is  sent when the
               Machine  White  and  Machine  Black  buttons   are
               selected.   This  is mostly for compatibility with
               previous versions of gnuchess.




X Version 11              June 11, 1991                         4





XBOARD(1)                                               XBOARD(1)


       XXBBooaarrdd**ffoonntt
               This is the font that is used by _x_b_o_a_r_d.

CCOOMMMMAANNDD BBUUTTTTOONNSS AANNDD KKEEYYSS
       QQuuiitt    Quits _x_b_o_a_r_d.  Q or q is a keyboard equivalent.

       RReesseett   Resets _x_b_o_a_r_d to the beginning of  a  chess  game.
               It also deselects any game or position files.

       FFlliipp VViieeww
               inverts the view of the chess board.

       HHiinntt    displays a move hint from GNU Chess.

       PPllaayy FFrroomm FFiillee
               plays  a  game  from a record file.  If no file is
               specified a popup  dialog  asks  for  a  filename.
               Game files are found in the directory named by the
               CHESSDIR environment variable.  If  this  variable
               is not declared then the current directory is used
               unless the file name starts with a /.  G or g is a
               keyboard equivalent.

       SSeettuupp FFrroomm FFiillee
               sets  up  a  position from a position file.  If no
               file is specified a popup dialog asks for a  file-
               name.   Position  files are found in the directory
               named by the CHESSDIR  environment  variable.   If
               this  variable  is  not  declared then the current
               directory is used unless the file name starts with
               a /.

       SSaavvee GGaammee
               saves  a  game  to  a  record file.  If no file is
               specified a popup dialog asks for a filename.

       SSaavvee PPoossiittiioonn
               saves a position to a position file.  If  no  file
               is specified a popup dialog asks for a filename.

       MMaacchhiinnee BBllaacckk
               forces GNU Chess to play black.

       MMaacchhiinnee WWhhiittee
               forces GNU Chess to play white.

       SSwwiittcchh SSiiddeess
               forces GNU Chess to switch sides.

       TTwwoo MMaacchhiinneess
               plays a game between two computer programs.

       FFoorrwwaarrdd moves  forward  through  a  series  of  remembered
               moves.  F or f is a keyboard equivalent.



